00:06:33.050 --> 00:06:35.190
and introduce it to everybody.

00:06:35.190 --> 00:06:40.650
So Cloud Run basically brings
serverless to containers.

00:06:40.650 --> 00:06:44.430
It allows you to run
any HTTP stateless

00:06:44.430 --> 00:06:47.880
workload on the
fully-serverless environment.

00:06:47.880 --> 00:06:49.550
MARK MIRCHANDANI: So
first things first,

00:06:49.550 --> 00:06:52.290
can you talk about, like, what
does serverless mean to you?

00:06:52.290 --> 00:06:54.623
STEREN GIANNINI: We define
serverless with the following

00:06:54.623 --> 00:06:55.590
characteristics.

00:06:55.590 --> 00:06:57.980
First and foremost, it's
an operational model.

00:06:57.980 --> 00:07:02.750
So you always use a
fully-managed infrastructure.

00:07:02.750 --> 00:07:05.060
You always pay for what you use.

00:07:05.060 --> 00:07:07.990
And you also have
a managed security.

00:07:07.990 --> 00:07:10.070
And when you think about
it, with that definition

00:07:10.070 --> 00:07:13.430
of serverless, you can realize
that it doesn't apply only

00:07:13.430 --> 00:07:15.570
to function as a service.

00:07:15.570 --> 00:07:18.140
It applies to even
more than just compute.

00:07:18.140 --> 00:07:20.810
If you take that definition
and look at something

00:07:20.810 --> 00:07:23.930
like Filestore, which is
a serverless database,

00:07:23.930 --> 00:07:25.190
it meets those requirements.

00:07:25.190 --> 00:07:28.880
And we qualify Cloud Filestore
as a serverless product

00:07:28.880 --> 00:07:29.990
for data.

00:07:29.990 --> 00:07:32.420
If we look at
serverless compute,

00:07:32.420 --> 00:07:35.360
we can refine a bit
more, the definition.

00:07:35.360 --> 00:07:38.720
We can add some
development model on top.

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:41.540
So when you develop for a
serverless compute environment,

00:07:41.540 --> 00:07:43.440
you use what we call services.

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:47.480
So it's more serverfull
than serverless actually.

00:07:47.480 --> 00:07:51.270
So you develop in term of
services-- maybe microservices.

00:07:51.270 --> 00:07:53.870
All of them are
independently scalable

00:07:53.870 --> 00:07:56.270
and they are stateless.

00:07:56.270 --> 00:07:59.840
So really, they autoscale
based on their needs.

00:07:59.840 --> 00:08:03.085
And more importantly, you only
pay for when you use them.

00:08:03.085 --> 00:08:04.460
And that applies
to everything we

00:08:04.460 --> 00:08:06.830
qualify as serverless,
including compute.

00:08:06.830 --> 00:08:09.110
When you don't send
any traffic or events

00:08:09.110 --> 00:08:11.960
to the function or
Cloud Run service,

00:08:11.960 --> 00:08:13.670
then you just
don't pay anything.

